35,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,The earlier works show a clear pattern of failure in hard surfaces.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Misaki,,"@Benjamin, the firms flagged clay subsoil. That explains the slippage risks.","{""words"":11,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Mio,,"The habitat fund only covers planting and water, not surfacing. That changes the budget.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Asuka,,We have only seven groundskeeping posts left. The volunteer groups are helpful but limited.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Minako,,The drainage callouts have doubled. The heat readings are also significantly higher.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"So, hard surfaces are a liability. We should avoid them.","{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Misaki,,"The depot notes say the south can be hoarded, but the center cannot.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Mio,,"@Benjamin, if we avoid hard surfaces, we save on the expensive upkeep.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"The volunteer groups are good for habitat, but not for heavy maintenance.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Minako,,"People prefer firm ground for crossing, but the drainage is failing.","{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"We need a plan that works with the soil, not against it.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Misaki,,A wetland or woodland plan might be more feasible given the soil risks.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Mio,,"The upkeep ledger confirms that planted ground is more expensive, but the fund helps.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"If we choose a plan that requires heavy maintenance, we will fail.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Minako,,The wetland plan addresses the drainage issue directly.,"{""words"":8,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,I am leaning towards a plan that uses the water management.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Misaki,,I agree. The earth-moving risks are too high for large structures.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Mio,,The habitat fund terms make the wetland plan financially viable.,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Asuka,,The volunteer groups can help with the habitat tasks upriver.,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Minako,,The wetland plan solves the drainage and heat issues.,"{""words"":9,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
